@startuml Composite-Object-Structure
title Composite — the resulting object structure (Design Patterns, p. 164)\nThe assembled PC of the Sample Code, as objects rather than classes

skinparam objectAttributeIconSize 0

object "cabinet : Cabinet" as cabinet {
  name = "PC Cabinet"
  ownNetPrice = $90.00
  netPrice() = $530.00
}

object "chassis : Chassis" as chassis {
  name = "PC Chassis"
  ownNetPrice = $210.00
  netPrice() = $440.00
}

object "bus : Bus" as bus {
  name = "MCA Bus"
  ownNetPrice = $75.00
  netPrice() = $195.00
}

object "card : Card" as card {
  name = "16Mbs Token Ring"
  netPrice() = $120.00
}

object "floppy : FloppyDisk" as floppy {
  name = "3.5in Floppy"
  netPrice() = $35.00
}

cabinet --> chassis
chassis --> bus
chassis --> floppy
bus --> card

note right of cabinet
  A client calls netPrice() here...
end note

note bottom of card
  ...and the recursion bottoms out
  at the leaves, which answer from
  their own state. Every intermediate
  node adds its own price to the sum
  of its children's.
end note

@enduml
